Getty 2026-11-19: "wir sollten noch in skeid einen modus einbauen der erlaubt das wenn man nur einen chat und einen embedding hat, das es dann quasi die model setting ignorieren kann und jedes model immer zu den richtigen führt".

Case: a node Skeid (e.g. synapse) offers exactly one chat model and one embedding model. Clients send whatever model name they were configured with (gpt-4o, qwen3, text-embedding-3-small, nomic-embed, …). Today that is a 404/400 unknown model. Wanted: the request goes to the right one by its kind.

Proposal (to be confirmed in an ADR):
- Config: `routing.catch_all: { chat: <model or alias>, embeddings: <model or alias> }` (maybe also `rerank`, `audio` later). Without the key nothing changes.
- The kind comes from the route, not from the name:
  - chat: /v1/chat/completions, /v1/completions, /v1/responses, /api/chat, /api/generate, Anthropic /v1/messages;
  - embeddings: /v1/embeddings, /api/embed, /api/embeddings.
- Only names that match no model and no alias are bent. Known names keep their normal routing, and the catch-all does not override policies: a key that may not use the target model still gets 403.
- Answer: the `model` field reports the real target. The usage event records both, requested_model and routed_model.
- /v1/models lists the real models and the aliases, not the catch-all; optionally a note in GET /skeid/config.
- Tests: chat and embedding routes with an unknown name, an Ollama route, a known name unchanged, policy refusal unchanged, the usage event with both names, and the config without catch_all byte-identical.

First user: synapse (chat → qwen3.8-flash-next-unc-q5, embeddings → qwen3-embedding-4b).

